# GitHub App Private Key Setup Instructions
# ============================================
#
# This private key file is obtained FROM GitHub after creating a GitHub App.
# You DO NOT create this file yourself - GitHub generates it for you.
#
# Steps to obtain this file:
# --------------------------
#
# 1. Create a GitHub App:
#    - Go to GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → GitHub Apps
#    - Click "New GitHub App"
#    - Fill in the required fields:
#      * Name: jenkins-ci (or similar, must be globally unique)
#      * Homepage URL: Your Jenkins URL
#      * Webhook URL: Your Jenkins URL + /github-webhook/
#    - Set Repository permissions:
#      * Contents: Read-only
#      * Metadata: Read-only
#      * Pull requests: Read & write (optional, for PR builds)
#      * Commit statuses: Read & write (optional, for build status)
#    - Click "Create GitHub App"
#
# 2. Generate and download the private key:
#    - After creating the app, scroll down to "Private keys"
#    - Click "Generate a private key"
#    - GitHub will automatically download a .pem file
#      (e.g., jenkins-ci.2025-10-24.private-key.pem)
#
# 3. Copy the downloaded file to your secrets directory:
#    cp ~/Downloads/jenkins-ci.YYYY-MM-DD.private-key.pem secrets/
#
# 4. Get your GitHub App ID:
#    - From the GitHub App settings page, note the "App ID" (a number)
#    - Add this to your .env file: GITHUB_APP_ID=123456
#
# 5. Install the GitHub App on your repository:
#    - On the GitHub App page, click "Install App"
#    - Select your account/organization
#    - Choose which repositories to grant access to
#    - Click "Install"
#
# 6. Update Jenkins configuration:
#    - The private key path in jenkins.yaml should match your .pem filename
#    - Rebuild and restart Jenkins: docker compose up -d --build
#
# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# ----------------
# - NEVER commit this file to Git (it's in .gitignore)
# - The .pem file is downloaded FROM GitHub, not uploaded TO GitHub
# - Keep this file secure - it authenticates your Jenkins as the GitHub App
# - If compromised, you can revoke and generate a new key from GitHub
# - The PKCS8 version is converted from the original .pem for Java compatibility
#
# File location: secrets/jenkins-ci.2025-10-24.private-key.pem
 